In PexGeneratedTest.cs, the generated Pex tests are defined. It tests all the public methods that throw exceptions, including exception throwing methods in the ArrayList class. Each method has a series of tests that cover all the different paths and combinations that may be executed by the method.

The output is in xml format, and you can then be run using any xml runner. Please note that you must have the NUnit framework installed to use the NUnit runner. You may also need to customize your runner settings according to specific requirements.

## Improving Coverage

To improve the testing coverage, you could use the following techniques:

- Increase the number of partitions and max testing iterations.
- Add more method contracts to the PexContractTest.cs file.
- Enable "partial trust" in PexSettings.xml by adding the “<PexSettings><RunPolicy>Partial</RunPolicy></PexSettings>” to your project.
- Use the static fields in your target classes by setting the StaticFieldInitialization property of the corresponding entries in the Settings.xml file to Static, or using the [PexUseRepresentativeValue] attribute to initialize fields.
- Using [PexMethodUnderTest] to apply more precise contracts.

