[PexMethodUnderTest] would be used for the method you want to test and PexAssumeUnderTest for your method's parameters. PexObserve is used to watch the values in the arrays to assert the inserted element at the proper position.

Also, `AssumePrecondition.IsTrue` is used to ensure some conditions are met regarding the method inputs. It'll prevent pex from creating tests that don't make sense, such as attempting to add an element to an index out of range.

Note: The PexContractTest.ArrayListContractTest class must be public and its methods must be public as well.

Also, note that Pex contracts will require a bit more setup and setup is required to verify if contracts are met.

**Also the Testing using Pex generates a large number of test cases, hence it is recommended to limit the size of the ArrayList while performing fuzz testing and also to test different corner cases.**

For detailed understanding consider checking the Microsoft documentation of Pex: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/test/how-to-specify-and-run-unit-tests-using-pex?view=vs-2019

Hope you find this helpful.
Happy testing.


 






  








